      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This work examines the coronary disease distribution in a large iron-foundry (7000 workers) with different ways of work and productive technologies, taking into consideration the high incidence and the multiple etiology of risk factors of cardiovascular diseases in the general population. In particular we studied the frequency of coronary disease and its consequence on the workers as far as retirement, death and job modification are concerned."},
